# olcli push/sync ignore list (gitignore syntax; see .claude/skills/overleaf).
#
# `olcli push` is manifest-based (tracks remote state in .olcli.json) but treats any
# file new locally as something to upload. data/ and figures/ are repo-side reproducibility
# scaffolding for the paper's figures (aggregate JSON symlinks, a uv project, rendered
# PDFs/PGFs) — none of it belongs in the Overleaf project, which only tracks the .tex/.sty
# sources. Without these entries, a bare `olcli push` from this directory would try to
# upload both trees (including the dangling scratch-wave3 symlinks) on the next sync.
data/
figures/
